{
  "Name": "Okta - Account & MFA Changes - Locked Out or Account Locked",
  "Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Account & MFA Changes\nMITRE ATT&CK: Credential Access / T1110\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Locked Out or Account Locked\" or \"<ip>|Locked Out or Account Locked\"\n\nFires on every Okta account lockout (user.account.lock, \"Max sign in attempts exceeded\") and on accounts that reached the lockout limit and will not unlock automatically (user.account.lock.limit). A lockout means the sign-on policy's failed-attempt limit was reached, which is what a brute-force or password-spray attack against the account produces.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_attempts_to_brute_force_okta_user_account/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/blob/main/rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_attempts_to_brute_force_okta_user_account.toml",
  "Labels": [
    "okta",
    "detection",
    "account-mfa-changes",
    "credential-access",
    "T1110"
  ],
  "Schedule": "7,22,37,52 * * * *",
  "Duration": -900,
  "DefaultDeploymentRules": {
    "Disabled": false,
    "RunImmediately": false
  },
  "ScheduledType": "search",
